ate of Kazan.", "newValue": "Qolşärif, a towering figure in the 16th-century Khanate of Kazan, served as a distinguished Old Tatar language-poet, influential statesman, esteemed university professor, and the chief imam of the Khanate, ultimately becoming a martyr during the Russian conquest. Born into a period of increasing Muscovite expansionism, his life, culminating in his death in 1552, epitomized the intellectual and spiritual resistance of the Volga Tatars against the encroaching Orthodox Christian power, solidifying his status as a pivotal cultural and religious leader in the region.

